{"availability":"available","full":"Keralots/BambuHelper","name":"BambuHelper","description":"ESP32 desk monitor for Bambu Lab printers. Real-time MQTT dashboard on a color TFT - temps, progress, fans, AMS, HMS errors. LAN or Cloud, dual printers, OTA, web config portal. Flash from the browser.","category":"Other","language":"C","stars":466,"forks":73,"created":"2026-03-07T16:27:12Z","updated":"2026-10-06T19:16:43Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://keralots.github.io/BambuHelper/","topics":["3d-printer","3d-printing","arduino","bambu-lab","bambulab","bambulabs","esp32","esp32-c3","esp32-s3","ili9341","iot","lovyangfx","mqtt","platformio","st7789","tft-display"],"demo":"https://keralots.github.io/BambuHelper/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:17.263Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:17.263Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:17.263Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:17.263Z","stars":466,"forks":73}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Dedicated Bambu Lab printer monitor built with ESP32-S3 Super Mini and a 1.54\" 240x240 color TFT display (ST7789).","Connects to your printer via MQTT over TLS and displays a real-time dashboard with arc gauges, animations, live stats, and optional buzzer notifications.","Additional supported boards include Guition JC3248W535 320x480, CYD 240x320, Waveshare ESP32-S3-Zero (with 240x240 or 240x320 panel), Waveshare 2\" 240x320, Waveshare 1.54\" 240x240, and ESP32-C3 DIY builds using the same 240x240 display as the ESP32-S3 version."],"features":["One-click web flasher - install firmware directly from keralots.github.io/BambuHelper in desktop Chrome/Edge - no PlatformIO, no esptool, no flash offsets","In-browser WiFi setup (Improv-Serial) - on first boot the install dialog asks for your WiFi over USB; no captive-portal switching needed (AP fallback still available)","Bambu account sign-in on the device - cloud setup without digging a token out of browser cookies: sign in with a password, an emailed code, or an authenticator app, then pick your printer from the account's own list","Live dashboard - progress arc, temperature gauges, fan speed, layer count, time remaining","H2-style LED progress bar - full-width glowing bar inspired by Bambu H2 series"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Keralots/BambuHelper/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"56baef4a2d27fa60f6428d855f4a4d255ef56e99e03b8383edeeb252039ad86e","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:17.407Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:17.407Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Dedicated Bambu Lab printer monitor built with ESP32-S3 Super Mini and a 1.54\" 240x240 color TFT display (ST7789).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Keralots/BambuHelper/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"With a remembered password the device signs in again on its own; otherwise you sign in again or paste a fresh token.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Keralots/BambuHelper/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Bambu account sign-in on the device - cloud setup without digging a token out of browser cookies: sign in with a password, an emailed code, or an authenticator app, then pick your printer from the account's own list","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Keralots/BambuHelper/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"Smart-plug power monitoring - per-printer Tasmota, Shelly Gen2/Gen3, Shelly Power Strip Gen4, or TP-Link Kasa legacy plug with live wattage, per-print kWh + cost, and optional auto-off after print finishes (with hot-end gate)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Keralots/BambuHelper/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Under Account access, either sign in with your Bambu account or paste an access token (see Connecting to Bambu Cloud below)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Keralots/BambuHelper/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind"